warning[G013]: count(*) counts 1, not 0, for stg_customers rows with no stg_orders row
 --> models/marts/customer_order_counts.sql:2:23
  |
2 | select c.customer_id, count(*) as order_count
  |                       ^^^^^^^^ counts rows of the left join, including unmatched stg_customers rows
  |
 ::: models/marts/customer_order_counts.sql:4:1
  |
4 | left join {{ ref('stg_orders') }} o on c.customer_id = o.customer_id
  | -------------------------------------------------------------------- left join keeps stg_customers rows with no stg_orders row
  |
  = note: the left join keeps each stg_customers row with no match once, with nulls for stg_orders; count(*) counts that row
  = help: count a column of stg_orders that is null on unmatched rows: count(o.customer_id)
  = see: cardinal explain G013

warning[G012]: UNION drops repeated rows, so equal amount values from different rows count once
 --> models/marts/money_movements.sql:3:1
  |
3 | union
  | ^^^^^ UNION keeps one copy of each set of equal rows
  |
  = note: branch 1 returns (customer_id, amount) from shop.payments, which can repeat: two different rows with the same values become one
  = note: it drops shop.payments's key (payment_id), which kept those rows apart
  = help: use UNION ALL to keep every row, or select (payment_id) so rows stay distinct
  = see: cardinal explain G012

warning[G014]: order_totals_by_customer keeps rows deleted in shop.orders: `_fivetran_deleted` is dropped without a filter
 --> models/marts/order_totals_by_customer.sql:3:6
  |
3 | from {{ ref('stg_orders_raw') }}
  |      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ reads every row of stg_orders_raw, deleted ones included
  |
  = note: shop.orders is synced with soft deletes: a row deleted at the source stays, with `_fivetran_deleted` set
  = note: stg_orders_raw keeps `_fivetran_deleted` without filtering on it, so its rows include deleted ones
  = note: this model doesn't select `_fivetran_deleted`, so nothing after it can filter deleted rows out
  = help: filter them out (where not coalesce(_fivetran_deleted, false)), or select `_fivetran_deleted` so a later model can; if keeping deleted rows is intended, add `-- cardinal: allow(G014) reason: …`
  = see: cardinal explain G014

