warning[G006]: snapshot unique_key (customer_id) isn't unique: the SQL can return several rows per (customer_id)
 --> snapshots/customers_snapshot.sql:6:1
  |
6 | join {{ source('shop', 'addresses') }} a on c.customer_id = a.customer_id
  | ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ one-to-many: rows repeat per row of shop.addresses, so (customer_id) repeats
  |
  = note: unique_key = customer_id, strategy: timestamp
  = note: two rows with the same (customer_id) in one run make the merge fail, or write two current versions; history written wrong can't be rebuilt, since the source has moved on
  = help: make the SQL return one row per (customer_id), e.g. with a row_number() dedup
  = see: cardinal explain G006

